WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
A car moves.

2
00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.090
It takes in fuel.

3
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.730
It uses oxygen, and it
gives out carbon dioxide.

4
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.170
It even gets warm as it runs.

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.150
Some cars can sense what's in
front of them and brake by

6
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.590
themselves.

7
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.490
Lots of living things
do all of that too.

8
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.950
So why isn't a car alive?

9
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.210
In this mission, you'll meet
the life processes that every

10
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.070
living organism carries out,

11
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.740
from movement and sensitivity
to growth and reproduction.

12
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.950
You'll find out what
each one really means:

13
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.210
how respiration releases energy,
what excretion gets rid of,

14
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.670
and what nutrition takes in.

15
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.780
Your mission: explain
why a car is not alive.
